# [DD-13b.W23.1] A COLUMN-1 `#` BETWEEN TWO INDENTED `config` BODY LINES.
# The comment TERMINATES the body exactly as a blank line does (r57 R2-F2),
# so the line BELOW it continues nothing and the file is refused THERE —
# measured rc 1 on the pre-W23 binary, and this fixture is what stops a
# future reader implementing the transparent reading (a comment is skipped
# and the structure around it continues), which would be a reject->accept
# widening.
#
# THE POSITION IS THE ASSERTION: the refusal must name the line below the
# comment, not the comment.
config dev
  flags i
# a column-one comment
  engine vm

pattern a+
m "aaa" 0 3
